---
layout: base.njk
title: Publications
description: >-
  HUBS Lab Papers, journal articles, and conference papers from the Human
  Building Synergy Laboratory at the University of Arizona.
---
{% from "icons.njk" import icon %}

{# Deliberately absent from site.nav — reached from the Research page, which is
   where someone looking for papers already is. The list itself is built from
   Dr. Jung's ORCID record at deploy time; see src/_data/publications.js. #}
<section class="pageHero wrap">
  <p class="label">Publications</p>
  <h1>Read the <span class="c-gold">work.</span></h1>
  <p class="lede">
    HUBS Lab Papers first, then everything published in journals and
    conferences, newest first. Each title goes to the paper; Cite downloads a
    citation file for your reference manager.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="band band--tight wrap">
  {#- The lab's own series, released on arXiv first, above the journal and
      conference papers. Its papers carry the series number rather than a place
      in the CV's count. One that goes on to a journal drops off by itself and
      its journal entry below carries the series number; see
      src/_data/publications.js. #}
  {%- set labPapers = publications | selectattr("lab") %}
  {%- if labPapers.length %}
  <div class="yearHead">
    <b>HUBS Lab Papers</b>
    <hr />
    <span>{{ labPapers.length }} {% if labPapers.length == 1 %}paper{% else %}papers{% endif %}</span>
  </div>

  <div class="labNote">
    <p>
      We release our work first, as a numbered series on arXiv, as soon as it
      is ready. The series is for work of journal scope; a short conference
      paper joins it only when its contribution to the community is large
      enough to stand on its own.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Speed.</b> In a field moving at the pace of AI, a year in review is
        a year the work is not being used, tested or challenged.</li>
      <li><b>Range.</b> Benchmarks, datasets, evaluation frameworks and careful
        negative or neutral results move the field forward, but rarely fit the shape of a
        journal article. The series gives them a permanent, citable home.</li>
      <li><b>A record of our own.</b> Each paper carries a series number and a
        permanent arXiv identifier, with its code and data archived alongside,
        in the way national laboratories publish their technical reports.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Many go on to journals and conferences; when one does, both versions are
      linked here. Some stand as lab papers in their own right. The series
      began in 2026, and we plan to bring the lab's work from earlier years
      into it as well.
    </p>
  </div>

  {#- Grouped by year under the heading. Some lab papers never go on to a
      journal, and without the year a three-year-old one would read as new. #}
  {%- for group in labPapers | groupPubsByYear %}
  <p class="pubsSub">{{ group.year }}</p>
  <ul class="pubs">
    {%- for p in group.items %}
    <li>
      <a class="pub__title" href="{{ p.doi }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ p.title }}</a>
      <p class="pub__authors">
        {%- for a in p.authors %}{{ a | authorDisplay }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </p>
      <p class="pub__meta">
        <span class="kind">{{ p.kind }}</span>
        <span>{{ p.venue }}</span>
        <a class="pub__doi" href="{{ p.doi }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ p.doi | replace("https://doi.org/", "") }}</a>
        <a class="pub__cite" href="/publications/{{ p.slug }}.ris" download>Cite</a>
      </p>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- endif %}

  {#- Set out the same way as the lab papers above: one heading for the group,
      the years as quiet labels beneath it. #}
  {%- set peerReviewed = publications | rejectattr("lab") %}
  <div class="yearHead">
    <b>Journal and Conference Papers</b>
    <hr />
    <span>{{ peerReviewed.length }} papers</span>
  </div>

  {%- for group in peerReviewed | groupPubsByYear %}
  <p class="pubsSub">{{ group.year }}</p>
  <ul class="pubs">
    {%- for p in group.items %}
    <li>
      <span class="pub__n" aria-hidden="true">{{ p.n }}</span>
      {%- if p.doi %}
      <a class="pub__title" href="{{ p.doi }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ p.title }}</a>
      {%- else %}
      {# No DOI was ever registered for this one, so there is nothing to link to. #}
      <span class="pub__title pub__title--plain">{{ p.title }}</span>
      {%- endif %}
      <p class="pub__authors">
        {%- for a in p.authors %}{{ a | authorDisplay }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </p>
      <p class="pub__meta">
        <span class="kind">{{ p.kind }}</span>
        <span>{{ p.venue }}{% if p.volume %}, {{ p.volume }}{% endif %}</span>
        {#- Shown bare rather than as a full URL: that is the form people paste
            into a reference manager, and it keeps the meta line short. #}
        {%- if p.doi %}
        <a class="pub__doi" href="{{ p.doi }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ p.doi | replace("https://doi.org/", "") }}</a>
        {%- endif %}
        {#- The arXiv copy this paper started as, linked for readers without a
            subscription. Set by src/_data/publications.js when a lab paper is
            matched to it. #}
        {%- if p.series %}
        <span>HUBS Lab Paper No. {{ p.series }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if p.arxiv %}
        <a class="pub__doi" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/{{ p.arxiv }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">arXiv:{{ p.arxiv }}</a>
        {%- endif %}
        <a class="pub__cite" href="/publications/{{ p.slug }}.ris" download>Cite</a>
      </p>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {%- endfor %}
</section>

<section class="band band--rule band--tight wrap">
  <div class="cta">
    <p class="label">Elsewhere</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.8rem">Citation counts.</h2>
    <div class="btnRow">
      <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="{{ site.social.scholar }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar {{ icon("external") }}</a>
      <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/research/">Research {{ icon("arrow-right") }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
